\v 1 When¦82265 the Day¦82275 of Pentecost¦82278 actually arrived, the believers met together¦82285 in the same¦82289 room¦82289.\x + \xo 2:1: \xt Lev 23:15-21; Deu 16:9-11.\x*
\v 2 Suddenly¦82293 there was a noise in the sky that sounded¦82297 like a strong¦82301 wind¦82300, then¦82290 it¦82304 filled¦82304 the entire¦82306 house¦82308 where¦82309 they¦82310 were sitting¦82312.
\v 3 They saw¦82314 what looked like tongues¦82317 of fire¦82319 that kept dividing¦82316\f + \fr 3:1 \ft See https://www.billmounce.com/monday-with-mounce/what-%E2%80%9Cdivided-tongue%E2%80%9D-acts-2-3-0\f* and¦82320 then¦82313 settling down on each one of them.
\v 4 In this way they were all filled¦82330 with the holy¦82334 spirit and¦82329 began¦82336 speaking in other¦82339 languages¦82340 as the spirit enabled them.
\p
\v 5 At the time, there were godly¦82360 Jews staying¦82356 in Yerushalem¦82353 that had come from other countries¦82365 all around the world.
\v 6 When¦82370 they heard this noise, lots of people¦82376 came¦82374 to investigate but¦82370 they were confused¦82378 because¦82380 they heard the believers talking¦82389 in their¦82393 own languages¦82388 \add from around the world\add*.
\v 7 They were astounded¦82394 and¦82398 marvelled¦82399, asking, “Wow, aren't¦82403 these¦82408 people talking¦82411 all Galileans¦82413?
\v 8 So¦82414 how come we're hearing¦82417 them speak the languages¦82422 of the countries where we were born¦82428?
\v 9 There's people here from Parthia¦82429, Media, Eylam, Mesopotamia¦82438, Yudea¦82439, Cappadocia¦82442, Pontus¦82443, Asia¦82446 \add Minor\add*,
\v 10 Frygia¦82451, Pamfylia¦82451, Egypt¦82451 \add !(Mitsrayim¦82451)\add*, Libya¦82457 (near Cyrene¦82460), and visitors¦82463 from Rome,
\v 11 Crete¦82470, and Arabia¦82472. Some are Jews and some are non-Jews who've converted¦82468 \add to Judaism\add*. And we¦82473 can hear¦82473 them talking¦82474 about \nd God¦82482\nd* in our¦82477 languages¦82478.”
\v 12 Everyone was amazed¦82483 and¦82486 totally puzzled, asking each other, “What's¦82497 going on here?”
\v 13 But others¦82504 scoffed¦82506 and said¦82509, “Ha, they've just had¦82514 too much to drink.”
\s1 Peter's sermon
\rem /s1 Peter Preaches to a Crowd; Peter Addresses the Crowd; Peter's Message
\p
\v 14 So the twelve stood¦82517 up and Peter¦82520 told the crowd in a loud voice¦82529, “People of Yudea and everyone staying¦82541 in Yerushalem¦82542. Listen to me so that¦82545 I can explain this to you.
\v 15 This group isn't¦82556 drunk¦82562 like you're all thinking¦82560, because¦82566 it's still mid-morning,
\v 16 but¦82573 you're seeing what the prophet¦82580 Yoel¦82581 wrote about:
\q1
\v 17 God said¦82590, ‘In the last¦82588 days¦82589 I'll¦82594 pour¦82594 out my¦82598 \nd spirit¦82597\nd* on all humanity—your children will tell¦82590 of future events, your young¦82617 men will see¦82621 visions¦82619, and¦82582 your old men will have dreams¦82627 \add from God\add*.\x + \xo 2:17-21: \xt Yoel 2:28-32 (LXX).\x*
\v 18 I'll¦82649 pour¦82649 my \nd spirit¦82652\nd* out on my male and female slaves¦82635 and they'll tell of future events.
\v 19 I'll¦82658 do unusual things with the stars and planets, and also down on the earth¦82668 below¦82669: blood¦82670, fire¦82672, and clouds of smoke¦82675.
\v 20 I'll make the sun¦82677 go dark and the moon¦82685 go blood¦82687 red. This will happen before¦82688 the great¦82695 victorious day¦82692 of the coming¦82690 of \nd Yahweh¦82693\nd*.
\v 21 Then¦82698 everyone¦82700 who relies on the name¦82706 and¦82698 authority of \nd Yahweh¦82708\nd* will be saved¦82709.’
\p
\v 22 “Fellow Israelis, listen¦82712 to this account: You yourselves¦82746 know¦82747 that¦82735 God did miracles¦82729 through \nd Yeshua\nd* from \nd Nazareth¦82718\nd*, and he fulfilled signs¦82733 \add from the scriptures\add*—in fact God did this right in front of you.
\v 23 Then as part of God's plan and foreknowledge¦82753, this Yeshua was taken to the authorities by those who didn't follow their own laws, and you¦82763 all¦82763 killed¦82763 him by having him \add nailed to\add*\x + \xo 2:23: \xt Jhn 20:25.\x* a post.\x + \xo 2:23: \xt Mat 27:35; Mrk 15:24; Luk 23:33; Yhn 19:18.\x*
\v 24 But \nd God¦82766\nd* released¦82768 him from the agonies¦82770 of death and brought him back to life—death couldn't restrain¦82778 him.\x + \xo 2:24: \xt Mat 28:5-6; Mrk 16:6; Luk 24:5.\x*
\v 25 As David¦82782 wrote,\x + \xo 2:25-28: \xt Psa 16:8-11 (LXX).\x*
\q1 ‘I foresaw¦82789 \nd Yahweh¦82791\nd* always being in front of me. I refuse to be afraid because¦82797 he's there on my¦82800 right¦82799.
