\v 28 You showed me the roads to life¦82847. You fill¦82848 me with gladness¦82850 because of your¦82855 presence¦82854.’
\p
\v 29 “Fellow Israelis, we can tell you¦82863 all¦82863 with confidence¦82861 that¦82885 our patriarch¦82866 David¦82867 both died¦82870 and was buried¦82872, and his¦82877 tomb¦82876 is still here with us today.
\v 30 So¦82887 because he was a prophet¦82886, and¦82889 knowing¦82891 that \nd God¦82897\nd* has¦82891 promised him to seat one of his descendants on his throne¦82916,\x + \xo 2:30: \xt Psa 132:11; 2Sam 7:12-13.\x*
\v 31 he was foretelling the resurrection¦82923 of the \nd messiah¦82925\nd* who was neither¦82927 ‘abandoned¦82929 in Hades¦82936 nor did his¦82941 body¦82940 decay¦82944.’
