\v 38 Peter¦83089 responded, “Turn away \add from your sins\add* and each one of you needs¦83098 to be immersed¦83098 by the authority of \nd Yeshua\nd* the \nd messiah¦83108\nd*. Then¦83090 your sins will be forgiven¦83110 and you¦83100 all¦83100 will receive¦83116 the gift¦83118 of the holy¦83120 \nd spirit¦83121\nd*,
\v 39 because¦83124 that promise¦83127 is to you¦83123 all¦83123 and your¦83132 children¦83130 and to their descendants—to anyone who will call¦83142 out to our¦83146 \nd God¦83145 Yahweh¦83143\nd*.”
\p
\v 40 Then Peter shared further teaching with them and¦83154 encouraged them to save¦83158 themselves out from this corrupt generation¦83161.
\v 41 Because of that, those who welcomed¦83170 his¦83174 teaching were immersed¦83175 and about¦83185 three¦83186 thousand¦83186 people were added¦83177 to their numbers that day¦83181.
\rem /s1 The Fellowship of the Believers
\v 42 They continued listening to the teaching¦83193 of the missionaries, and building their relationships with each other, and breaking¦83203 bread¦83205 and praying together.
\s1 The lifestyle of the early believers
