\p
\v 1 One afternoon around 3pm, Peter¦83332 and¦83333 Yohan¦83339 were going¦83340 to the prayer¦83352 meeting in the temple¦83343.
\v 2 Now there was a man¦83359 who had been lame¦83360 from birth, and¦83356 every¦83370 day¦83371 he was placed beside a door¦83374 into the temple—an entry named ‘Beautiful¦83379 Door’. From there he could beg from the people entering¦83386 the temple.
\v 3 He saw¦83398 Peter¦83399 and¦83400 Yohan¦83401 about to enter¦83404 into the temple¦83407, so he asked¦83408 them for a donation,
\v 4 but¦83415 Peter¦83417 and Yohan¦83423, looking¦83414 closely at him¦83420 said¦83426, “Look at us!”
\v 5 So¦83432 the man grabbed onto them, expecting¦83436 to get given something¦83437 by them.
\v 6 But¦83450 Peter¦83447 said¦83443, “I don't¦83452 have any silver or gold¦83451, but¦83445 I'll give¦83460 you what I do have. With the authority of \nd Yeshua\nd* the \nd messiah¦83465\nd* from \nd Nazareth¦83467\nd*, \add I command you\add* to walk¦83471.”
\v 7 Then¦83472 Peter grabbed¦83473 the man by the right¦83476 hand¦83477 and pulled him upwards. Immediately¦83481 the man's feet¦83488 and ankles¦83493 were strengthened¦83485
\v 8 and he jumped up and stood¦83496 and started walking and went¦83501 into the temple¦83506 with them, walking and skipping and praising¦83511 \nd God¦83513\nd*.
\v 9 All the people¦83519 \add there\add* saw¦83515 him¦83520 walking¦83521 and¦83522 praising¦83523 \nd God¦83526\nd*,
\v 10 and recognising¦83527 that he was the man who usually sat¦83541 \add outside\add* begging at the ‘Beautiful¦83545 Door’ of the temple¦83550, they were astonished and astounded at what had¦83560 happened¦83560 to him.
\s1 Peter's sermon in the temple
\rem /s1 Peter Speaks to the Onlookers; Peter's Message in the Temple; Peter Speaks in Solomon's Portico
\p
\v 11 As the man clung onto Peter¦83572 and Yohan¦83576, all the people¦83585 ran¦83578 to see them in Solomon's¦83599 Porch and they were really astounded¦83600.
\rem /s1 Peter Preaches in the Temple
\v 12 But when Peter¦83605 saw¦83602 \add the crowd\add*, he answered¦83607 their thoughts¦83623, “Fellow Israelis¦83611, why are you¦83615 all¦83615 puzzled about this, and why are you staring at us as if this man is walking¦83636 because of \em our\em* power¦83627 or closeness to God.”
\v 13 The god of Abraham¦83640, Isaac¦83644, and Yacob¦83648—the god of our¦83654 fathers¦83653—gave¦83666 honour to his¦83659 servant¦83658, \nd Yeshua\nd*, who you handed over \add to be killed\add* and then you rejected him when Pilate¦83675 had¦83677 judged¦83677 him and wanted to release him.\x + \xo 3:13: \xt Exo 3:15.\x*
