\v 8 And he contracted with Abraham about being circumcised, and so when Abraham had Isaac, he circumcised him on the eighth¦86400 day¦86397, and then¦86383 Isaac went on to have Yacob, and Yacob to have the \add twelve\add* tribal leaders.\x + \xo 7:8: a \xt Gen 17:10-14; \xo b \xt Gen 21:2-4; \xo c \xt Gen 25:26; \xo d \xt Gen 29:31–35:18.\x*
\p
\v 9 Those brothers went on to become jealous¦86415 of Yosef and¦86412 sent him back into Egypt¦86420 \add as a slave\add*, but¦86412 \nd God¦86424\nd* was with him\x + \xo 7:9: a \xt Gen 37:11; \xo b \xt Gen 37:28; \xo c \xt Gen 39:2,21.\x*
\v 10 and rescued¦86428 him out of all his¦86434 troubles there. Then God gave¦86436 him wisdom¦86441 and caused him to gain the favour¦86438 of \add Far'oh (Pharaoh)\add*, the king¦86445 of Egypt, who then appointed¦86448 him as the ruler of all Egypt and over Far'oh's own household¦86457.\x + \xo 7:10: \xt Gen 41:39-41.\x*
