\v 32 ‘I am the god of your¦86905 ancestors¦86904—the god of Abraham¦86908 and of Isaac¦86912 and of Yacob¦86916.’ At that point, Mosheh¦86921 started trembling¦86917 and was scared to go any closer to look,
\v 33 but¦86931 \nd Yahweh¦86936\nd* said¦86928, ‘Take off your¦86945 sandals¦86940, because¦86947 the ground¦86956 you're standing¦86955 on is dedicated to God.
\v 34 I have noticed¦86962 the mistreatment¦86964 of my¦86967 people¦86966 in Egypt and heard¦86976 their¦86974 groaning¦86973 and so I came¦86979 down to rescue¦86980 them, so now I'm going to send¦86985 you¦86987 \add back\add* to Egypt.’
\p
\v 35 This was the same Mosheh¦86992 that they¦86994 had previously rejected and asked who had made him ruler and judge¦87001 over them. Now \nd God¦87006\nd* had indeed sent¦87014 him as ruler and liberator by means of the messenger¦87018 that he saw¦87020 in the thorn¦87024 bush.\x + \xo 7:35: \xt Exo 2:14.\x*
\v 36 So eventually Mosheh led¦87026 them out of Egypt¦87036 after doing¦87029 miracles and signs¦87032 of God's power there, and then also at the Red Sea and during the forty¦87047 years¦87046 in the wilderness¦87045.\x + \xo 7:36: a \xt Exo 7:3; \xo b \xt Exo 14:21; \xo c \xt Num 14:33.\x*
