\v 26 Then a messenger¦88099 from \nd Yahweh¦88101\nd* spoke¦88102 to Philip¦88104, “Start walking and¦88108 head south¦88112 on the road that¦88118 goes¦88109 downhill from Yerushalem¦88122 to Gaza¦88124 through the wilderness¦88127.”
\v 27 So¦88128 he headed off, and¦88128 \add on the road\add* he came across an important official¦88136 of the Ethiopian¦88134 queen\f + \fr 8:27 \ft Some translations list the queen's name as ‘Candace’, but that was the name of the series of queens, cf., Far'oh (Pharaoh) or Caesar which came to be used as a title for more than one person.\f* who was in charge of her¦88148 treasury¦88147. This man¦88133 had¦88151 been in Yerushalem¦88154 to worship God
