\p
\v 37 ◘
\v 38 So¦88366 he commanded¦88367 \add the driver\add* to stop¦88368 the chariot¦88370 and they¦88372 both climbed down, and Philip¦88379 immersed¦88384 the official in the water¦88376.
\v 39 But¦88404 as they¦88388 came out of the water¦88391, \nd Yahweh's spirit¦88392\nd* snatched¦88401 Philip¦88403 away and¦88404 so the official never saw¦88406 him again, but¦88387 he continued on his¦88416 journey very happy.
\v 40 As for Philip¦88418, he found¦88420 himself at \add the town of\add* Azotus¦88422, and¦88423 as he passed¦88424 through¦88424 \add the coastal towns\add* on the way to Caesarea¦88435, he proclaimed the good¦88425 message¦88425 in each town.
\c 9
\s1 Yeshua talks to Saul
\rem /s1 The Conversion of Saul; Saul's Conversion
