\v 11 So¦88647 the \nd master¦88648\nd* told him¦88650, “Get up and¦88660 go to Yudas' house¦88663 in Straight¦88659 Street¦88656 where you'll find a man named Saul¦88665 from Tarsus¦88667. He's praying¦88670 right now
\v 12 and in his vision¦88675, he saw¦88672 a man¦88673 named Ananias¦88678 who comes¦88680 in and places his hands¦88686 on him¦88683 so that he can receive¦88688 his sight¦88688 back.”
\p
\v 13 But¦88690 Ananias¦88692 resisted, “\nd Master¦88693\nd*, I've heard¦88695 a lot about that¦88701 man¦88700, including all the evil¦88703 things he's done¦88708 to your¦88707 dedicated people in Yerushalem¦88710,
\v 14 and¦88712 the reason he's here in Damascus with the authority¦88715 of the chief¦88718 priests¦88718 is to arrest everyone who trusts in you¦88725.”
\p
\v 15 But¦88752 the \nd master¦88731\nd* said¦88726, “Go now, because¦88733 I've chosen that¦88740 man¦88739 to be a bearer of my¦88744 name¦88743 and authority both in other countries, even to their kings¦88750, and to the descendants of Yisrael¦88753,
\v 16 because¦88755 I'll¦88754 be showing¦88756 him what he's going to have to suffer¦88765 for bearing my¦88764 name¦88763.”
\p
\v 17 So¦88768 Ananias¦88769 left and went¦88766 into Yudas' house¦88774 where he placed¦88776 his hands¦88780 on Saul and said¦88783, “Brother¦88785 Saul, the \nd master¦88787\nd* has¦88788 sent¦88788 me here—\nd Yeshua\nd* the one you saw on the road¦88796 when you were coming¦88798 here—so that¦88797 you'll be able to see again and also be filled¦88803 with the holy¦88805 \nd spirit¦88804\nd*.”
\v 18 Immediately¦88807 something¦88808 like scales¦88816 fell¦88808 off Saul's eyes¦88812 and he was able to see again, and he got up¦88823 and got immersed¦88825 in water,
\v 19 before getting something to eat to renew his strength¦88830.
\s1 Saul starts preaching in Damascus
\rem /s1 Saul Preaches in Damascus; Saul in Damascus and Jerusalem
\p Then¦88832 Saul stayed several days¦88840 with the believers in Damascus¦88838.
