\p
\v 22 But¦88902 Saul was growing stronger\f + \fr 9:22 \ft It's not clear here whether it means that Saul was growing physically stronger, or that his preaching and debating skills were improving.\f* and he was confounding¦88903 the Jews living¦88907 in Damascus¦88909 as he taught¦88910 them that Yeshua is the \add promised\add* \nd messiah¦88915\nd*.
\rem /s1 Saul Escapes from the Jews
\p
\v 23 After several days¦88919, the religious Jews plotted¦88921 together¦88921 to kill¦88924 him¦88925,\x + \xo 9:23-25: \xt 2Cor 11:32-33.\x*
\v 24 but¦88935 Saul¦88929 found out about their¦88932 plan. Those Jews were also watching¦88934 the city exits so they¦88949 could¦88949 kill¦88949 him¦88948 if he tried leaving,
\v 25 but¦88951 his¦88955 supporters took¦88950 him to the city wall¦88961 at night¦88956 time and¦88951 lowered¦88964 him down in a basket¦88966.
\s1 Saul goes to Yerushalem but has to leave
