\p
\v 26 When¦88969 he got back to Yerushalem¦88974, Saul attempted¦88976 to join in with the believers there but¦88981 they were all scared of him¦88984, not believing¦88986 that he was a true follower¦88980 of Yeshua.
\v 27 However Barnabas¦88990 took¦88992 Saul and brought¦88994 him to the twelve, and Saul told them how he had seen¦89005 the \nd master¦89007\nd* on the road¦89004, and been spoken to by him, and how he had spoken boldly¦89016 in Damascus¦89015 in the name¦89019 and authority of \nd Yeshua\nd*.
\v 28 So¦89023 Saul stayed connected with the believers, going¦89029 in and out of Yerushalem¦89032 and speaking¦89035 boldly¦89035 in the name¦89038 and authority of the \nd master¦89040\nd*.
\v 29 He also talked and¦89044 debated¦89045 with the Greek-speaking Jews, but¦89052 they¦89051 wanted to kill¦89055 him¦89056,
\v 30 so when the brothers¦89061 found out, they¦89068 took Saul down to Caesarea¦89066 \add on the coast\add*, and¦89067 from there sent¦89068 him \add on a ship\add* to Tarsus¦89072.
\p
\v 31 After that the assemblies¦89078\f + \fr 9:31 \ft Lit. ‘assembly’ (singular). Jonathan Leeman in ‘One Assembly’ makes a good case that the force of κατά ‘throughout’ contributes to making the force of ἐκκλησία plural in this sentence (similar to Luke's use in Luke 4:14, 23:5, Acts 9:42, 10:37).\f* of believers throughout Yudea¦89082 and Galilee¦89084 and Shomron¦89086 \add !(Samaria¦89086)\add* had¦89087 peace¦89089 and grew in their respect and service of the \nd master¦89099\nd*, as well as increasing in numbers through the encouragement of the holy¦89104 \nd spirit¦89105\nd*.
\s1 Peter heals Aeneas
\rem /s1 Aeneas and Dorcas; Peter in Lydda and Joppa; The Healing of Aeneas; Peter Heals Aeneas and Raises Dorcas
\p
\v 32 Peter¦89110 travelled around the country and¦89109 then¦89109 went to visit the dedicated believers in Lydda¦89122.
\v 33 He saw a paralysed¦89141 man¦89127 named Aeneas who'd spent eight¦89134 years¦89133 lying¦89135 on his pallet¦89138,
\v 34 and said¦89143 to him¦89144, “Aeneas, \nd Yeshua\nd* the \nd messiah¦89154\nd* is healing¦89148 you¦89149. Stand up and pack up your bed¦89157.” And straight away Aeneas stood up
\v 35 and all the people living¦89168 in Lydda¦89169 and Sharon¦89173 who saw¦89163 him¦89165 became followers of the \nd master¦89178\nd*.
\s1 Peter brings Tabitha back to life
\rem /s1 Peter in Lydda and Joppa
\p
\v 36 Then¦89181 in Yafo¦89180 \add !(Joppa¦89180)\add* there was a believer named Tabitha¦89186 (or Dorcas if translated) and¦89197 she¦89200 did¦89200 a lot of good¦89196 things as well as being generous to the poor.
\v 37 Around that time¦89205 she¦89208 got sick and¦89202 died¦89209. After washing her¦89212 body, they¦89213 placed it¦89201 in an upper¦89217 room¦89217,
\v 38 and since Yafo¦89224 was near Lydda¦89221 and the believers had¦89227 heard¦89227 that Peter¦89229 was there, they¦89233 quickly sent¦89233 two¦89234 men¦89235 to request, “Please come as soon as possible.”
\v 39 So¦89247 Peter¦89249 went¦89250 with them, and when they arrived¦89253 in Yafo they took him up to the room¦89259. All the widows¦89265 stood¦89261 there, sobbing and showing¦89268 him various clothes¦89271 that Tabitha had made¦89273 for them.
\v 40 But¦89308 Peter had them all removed from the room, and then¦89308 kneeling¦89295 down he prayed¦89298 before turning¦89300 back to the body¦89303 and said¦89304, “Tabitha¦89305, get up.” Then¦89308 she opened¦89309 her¦89312 eyes¦89311, and seeing¦89314 Peter there she sat¦89317 up.
\v 41 Peter helped her to stand up, then¦89320 he called¦89326 the believers and the widows¦89332, and presented¦89336 the live¦89338 Tabitha to them.
\v 42 News of this spread throughout¦89342 Yafo¦89345 and¦89346 many people there believed¦89348 in the \nd master¦89352\nd*.
\v 43 So¦89354 Peter¦89362 stayed on there for quite a few days¦89356, living with a tanner¦89366 of hides named Simon¦89365.
\c 10
\s1 Peter and Cornelius each hear from God
\rem /s1 Peter and Cornelius; Cornelius Calls for Peter
\p
\v 1 Just up in Caesarea¦89372 there was a Roman army commander named Cornelius¦89374 (leader of the ‘Italian¦89380 Regiment’)
\v 2 who, along with all his household¦89389, worshipped God and obeyed his laws. He gave to the poor and regularly asked God for help.
\v 3 One afternoon around 3pm he had a vision¦89405 where he clearly¦89406 saw¦89403 one of God's messengers¦89414 come¦89417 into the house and¦89420 call, “Cornelius¦89423.”
\p
\v 4 Cornelius was scared and looked¦89426 intently¦89426 and asked, “What is it¦89434, master¦89435?”
\p “Your¦89441 prayers¦89440 and your¦89441 helping the poor rose up to God's notice and attention,” he said.
\v 5 “Now, send some messengers to Yafo¦89458 to go and¦89453 find a man there named Simon¦89462 Peter¦89469.
\v 6 He's staying with Simon¦89474 the tanner¦89476 whose¦89477 house¦89480 is by the sea¦89482.”
\v 7 So¦89491 as soon as the messenger¦89494 left, Cornelius called¦89500 two¦89501 of his house¦89503 servants¦89503 and¦89505 a godly¦89507 soldier¦89506 from his bodyguard,
\v 8 and¦89511 after explaining¦89512 the task to them, he sent¦89518 them off to Yafo¦89522.
\rem /s1 Peter's Vision; Peter Visits Cornelius
\p
\v 9 The next¦89525 day¦89523 as they were approaching the town¦89531, Peter¦89534 went¦89533 up onto the flat roof¦89537 of the house¦89537 around midday to pray¦89538.
\v 10 But¦89547 he felt hungry¦89546 and¦89547 wanted¦89548 something to eat, but¦89545 while it was still being prepared¦89550 he fell into a trance¦89560
\v 11 and saw the sky open¦89565 up. Something like a sheet¦89573 was being¦89581 lowered down to the earth¦89584 by the four¦89575 corners¦89576
\v 12 and it held all kinds of animals and reptiles¦89598, as well as birds¦89603.
\v 13 Then¦89606 he heard a voice¦89608 saying, “Get up Peter¦89612, and slaughter these and eat¦89615 them.”
\p
\v 14 “I can't, \nd master¦89621\nd*,” Peter¦89618 responded¦89619, “because¦89622 I've never¦89623 eaten anything that's forbidden.”
\p
\v 15 But¦89630 the voice¦89631 spoke a second¦89636 time¦89636, “Don't¦89645 you¦89643 be treating anything as unclean that \nd God¦89641\nd* has made clean¦89642.”
\v 16 This vision happened three¦89651 times and¦89652 then¦89648 the sheet thing was lifted back up into the sky.
\p
\v 17 Now¦89694 Peter¦89670 was still there wondering what the vision¦89676 was all about when the men¦89682 sent¦89684 by Cornelius¦89688 had tracked down the tanner's house¦89692 and¦89663 arrived outside.
\v 18 They called out to ask if Simon¦89704 Peter¦89707 was staying there.
\p
\v 19 Even as Peter¦89712 still continued¦89718 to ponder¦89714 about¦89715 the vision¦89717, the \nd spirit¦89722\nd* said¦89718, “Hey, there's three¦89727 men¦89725 here looking¦89728 for¦89728 you¦89730.
\v 20 So get up and¦89735 go¦89736 downstairs to them. Believe everything they say because¦89743 I sent¦89746 them here.”
\v 21 So¦89750 he went down and¦89750 asked the men¦89756, “I'm the one you're looking¦89769 for, so tell me what you came¦89778 here for.”
\p
\v 22 They answered, “We were sent by Cornelius¦89784 who's an army commander who worships \nd God¦89792\nd* and obeys his laws and has a good reputation with you Jewish people. A holy¦89805 messenger¦89804 told him¦89811 to send¦89806 for you to come to his house¦89810 so they¦89779 can listen¦89813 to what you have to say¦89781.”
\v 23 So¦89827 Peter invited them in to stay the night.
\rem /s1 Peter at Cornelius' House
\p The next¦89828 day¦89826, Peter and¦89835 some of the believers¦89838 from Yafo¦89842 started out with them
\v 24 and they arrived in Caesarea¦89854 the following day¦89847. Cornelius¦89857 was expecting¦89860 them and had¦89863 also invited some relatives¦89865 and close¦89870 friends¦89871 to join them.
\v 25 Peter¦89881 entered the house and when they met¦89894, Cornelius¦89898 knelt down and worshipped him
\v 26 but¦89911 Peter¦89912 pulled him¦89915 up and said¦89916, “Stand up. I'm just a man like you.”
\v 27 After they greeted each other, Peter went¦89933 into the main room and¦89937 found¦89938 that quite a few people had¦89940 gathered there.
\v 28 Then¦89943 he told them, “You¦89946 all¦89946 know¦89948 that us Jews are forbidden by our laws to associate with or to enter the house of a non-Jew. However, \nd God¦89966\nd* showed¦89968 me that it's not right to treat other¦89959 people as being¦89955 lesser or undesirable.
\v 29 That's why I came¦89978 without any reservations when you sent for me. But I'm still waiting to know what you¦89987 all¦89987 want from me?”
\p
\v 30 So¦89989 Cornelius¦89992 answered, “I was praying¦90013 in my¦90017 house¦90016 three days ago in the middle of the afternoon when I suddenly saw¦90019 a man¦90020 in shining¦90026 clothes¦90025 standing¦90021 in front of me
\v 31 and he said¦90028, ‘Your¦90032 prayer¦90035 has been heard, Cornelius¦90029, and \nd God¦90046\nd* has noticed your¦90032 gifts to the poor.
\v 32 Now he wants you to send¦90047 messengers to get Simon, the one called¦90055 Peter¦90056, from Yafo¦90050 where he's living by the sea¦90069 in Simon the tanner's¦90065 house¦90061.’
\v 33 I did¦90088 that straight away and¦90086 you kindly came here, so now we're all here in God's \add sight\add* to find out everything that the \nd master¦90115\nd* has commanded¦90109 you to say.”
\s1 Peter's talk in Caesarea
\rem /s1 Gentiles Hear the Good Message; The Gentiles Hear the Good News; Peter's Speech
\p
\v 34 So¦90118 Peter¦90119 spoke up and¦90118 said¦90124, “Honestly, I'm still just realising that \nd God¦90134\nd* doesn't favour¦90132 only certain people,\x + \xo 10:34: \xt Deu 10:17.\x*
\v 35 but¦90142 he accepts¦90145 people from any nation¦90138 as long as they honour and¦90142 obey him.
\v 36 He sent¦90153 us a message through the descendants of Yisrael¦90156—a good¦90157 message that teaches that we can have peace¦90159 through \nd Yeshua\nd* the \nd messiah¦90162\nd*—everyone's \nd master¦90166\nd*.
\v 37 And you¦90167 all¦90167 know¦90168 the news that started in Galilee¦90182 and spread through¦90173 all Yudea¦90176 after¦90183 the time of Yohan's teaching and ministry of immersion¦90185—
\v 38 how God filled \nd Yeshua\nd* from \nd Nazareth¦90192\nd* with the holy¦90200 \nd spirit¦90199\nd* and with power¦90203, and who then went around doing¦90209 good¦90209 and healing¦90211 all those oppressed¦90214 by the devil¦90218, because¦90219 God was with him.
\v 39 We are witnesses¦90230 of all the things he did¦90234 in the Jewish provinces and in Yerushalem¦90243, and then¦90225 how they¦90246 executed him \add by nailing him to\add*\x + \xo 10:39: \xt Jhn 20:25.\x* a stake¦90249.
\v 40 Then \nd God¦90252\nd* brought him back to life on the third¦90258 day¦90260 and¦90262 sent him where he could be seen,
\v 41 not by all the people¦90271, but¦90284 to the witnesses¦90273 that¦90274 \nd God¦90279\nd* had¦90275 previously¦90275 appointed¦90275—to us who ate¦90282 with him and¦90284 drank¦90285 with him after¦90289 he'd been raised from the dead¦90294.
\v 42 He commanded¦90299 us to tell the people¦90303, and to testify¦90305 that¦90307 he is the one who \nd God¦90314\nd* has¦90311 designated¦90311 to be the judge¦90315 of the living¦90316 and the dead¦90318.
\v 43 \add The writings of\add* all the prophets¦90322 point towards him, and everyone¦90331 who believes¦90333 \add that he's God\add* can have their sins¦90325 forgiven¦90324 by his¦90330 authority.”
\s1 God's spirit enters non-Jews
\rem /s1 The Gentiles Receive the Holy Spirit
\p
\v 44 While Peter¦90339 was still¦90336 speaking¦90337, the holy¦90348 \nd spirit¦90346\nd* came down onto everyone who was listening.
\v 45 The Jewish believers¦90360 who had come¦90363 with Peter¦90365 were astonished that the gift¦90372 of the holy¦90374 \nd spirit¦90375\nd* had been poured¦90378 out even on non-Jews
\v 46 as they¦90379 heard¦90379 them speaking¦90382 in other languages¦90383 and¦90384 magnifying¦90385 \nd God¦90387\nd*. Then Peter¦90393 said,
\v 47 “Surely¦90394 no one could argue against them getting immersed¦90404 in water¦90396 now that¦90402 they've received¦90412 the holy¦90411 \nd spirit¦90409\nd* just like we¦90417 did¦90417?”
\v 48 So with the authority of \nd Yeshua\nd* the \nd messiah¦90431\nd*, he commanded¦90419 for them to be immersed¦90432 \add in water\add*. Then they¦90435 asked¦90435 him¦90436 to stay with them for a few more days¦90441.
\c 11
\s1 Peter explains everything to those in Yerushalem
\rem /s1 Peter Explains His Actions; Peter's Report to the Church at Jerusalem
\p
\v 1 Soon the missionaries and¦90451 other believers¦90454 in Yudea¦90462 heard¦90444 that¦90456 non-Jews had also accepted God's message¦90471,
\v 2 but¦90478 when Peter¦90481 went¦90480 to Yerushalem¦90488, the strict Jewish believers were upset with him¦90523,
\v 3 saying¦90527 that he had¦90534 gone into the home of uncircumcised¦90533 pagans and¦90536 \add even\add* eaten with them.
\p
\v 4 But Peter¦90544 started explaining¦90545 from the beginning¦90541,
\v 5 “I was staying in Yafo¦90554, and as I was praying¦90556 I saw¦90558 a vision¦90561 of an object¦90564 like a sheet¦90567 coming¦90562 down, as if it was being¦90571 let down out of the sky by its¦90569 four¦90569 corners¦90570. As it came¦90577 down to me
\v 6 I looked¦90583 at it and saw¦90586 animals, even wild¦90593 animals, and reptiles¦90596 and birds¦90599.
\v 7 I also heard¦90603 a voice¦90606 telling me, ‘Peter¦90613, get up and slaughter these and eat¦90616 them.’
\v 8 But I said¦90617, ‘\nd Master¦90620\nd*, I can't because¦90621 I've never¦90627 eaten anything that's forbidden.’
\v 9 But the voice¦90637 from the sky spoke again, ‘Don't¦90651 you¦90650 be treating anything as unclean that \nd God¦90648\nd* has made clean¦90649.’
\v 10 This happened three¦90657 times, and¦90658 then¦90654 it was pulled¦90660 up again into the sky.
\v 11 Next minute there were three¦90669 men¦90670 at the house¦90675 where I was staying \add saying\add* that¦90677 they had¦90680 been sent¦90680 from Caesarea¦90682 to fetch me,
\v 12 and the \nd spirit¦90689\nd* told¦90685 me to go with them without questioning anything they said. These six¦90703 other believers¦90704 went¦90697 with me, and we¦90707 arrived at the house¦90710 of the man¦90712 \add who had sent the three\add*.
\v 13 He told us how he'd seen¦90718 one \add of God's\add* messengers¦90720 standing¦90725 there in his¦90724 house¦90723 and who'd told him¦90724, ‘Send¦90735 \add someone\add* to Yafo¦90732 to fetch Simon¦90736, the one called¦90738 Peter¦90739,
\v 14 and he will explain to you how you and all your¦90754 household¦90753 can be saved¦90748.’
\v 15 Then¦90756 when I started speaking¦90760 to them, the holy¦90767 \nd spirit¦90765\nd* came down on them just like it had happened to us previously.
\v 16 That reminded¦90778 me of the words of the \nd master¦90784\nd* when he told us, ‘Yohan¦90787 immersed people in water¦90790, but¦90780 you¦90791 all¦90791 will be immersed in the holy¦90797 \nd spirit¦90795\nd*.
\v 17 Therefore¦90799 if God gave¦90803 the same¦90801 gift¦90802 to them that he'd given to us when we'd believed¦90811 in the \nd master¦90814 Yeshua\nd* the \nd messiah¦90816\nd*, what authority did I have¦90811 to contradict God?’ ”
\p
\v 18 When¦90835 the group heard¦90834 all this, they had no objections and they praised God, saying¦90844, “It seems that God has also allowed the pagans¦90849 to repent¦90853 and live.”
\s1 Many in Antioch become believers
\rem /s1 The Church at Antioch; The Church in Antioch of Syria
\p
\v 19 Over time, due to the persecution that¦90865 began with Stephen's killing, the ones who had moved away went as far as Phoenicia¦90874, Cyprus¦90876, and Antioch¦90878, but¦90875 they only shared Yeshua's teaching with other Jews.
\v 20 However, some of the believers were from Cyprus and Cyrene¦90898, and when they got to Antioch¦90903 they proclaimed the good¦90911 news from the \nd master¦90913 Yeshua\nd* to the Greeks.
\v 21 \nd Yahweh¦90920\nd* caused their efforts to prosper, so a large¦90923 number¦90925 of Greeks believed¦90927 and¦90916 decided to follow the master.
\p
\v 22 News about this reached the assembly¦90940 in Yerushalem¦90944, so they¦90949 sent¦90949 Barnabas¦90950 to Antioch¦90954.
\v 23 When he arrived¦90957 and saw¦90959 how God's grace¦90961 \add was spreading\add*, he was elated¦90965 and encouraged them all to earnestly continue to follow the \nd master¦90976\nd*.
\v 24 Barnabas was good¦90981 man¦90979 and full of the holy¦90985 \nd spirit¦90984\nd* and full of faith¦90987 \add in God\add*, and a large¦90991 number of people decided to follow Yeshua.
\p
\v 25 So¦90996 Barnabas went¦90995 to Tarsus¦91001 to look for Saul¦91009,
\v 26 and when he found¦91012 him, he brought¦91015 him back to Antioch. Then¦91024 for a whole¦91029 year¦91028 they met with the assembly¦91034 and \add regularly\add* taught¦91037 a large¦91039 crowd¦91038. It was there in Antioch that the believers were first¦91044 called¦91040 Christians.
\p
\v 27 In those days¦91064, some prophets¦91068 from Yerushalem¦91067 went¦91065 to Antioch¦91070,
\v 28 and one of them named Agabus¦91085 when he was prompted by the \nd spirit¦91091\nd*, stood¦91079 up and predicted that¦91102 the world¦91101 would experience a severe famine¦91092 (and this happened \add later\add* during¦91106 the reign of Claudius¦91107).
\v 29 The believers decided to send¦91125 assistance to their¦91122 fellow¦91131 believers who lived in Yudea¦91130—each one according to his means—
\v 30 and so they¦91136 did¦91136, sending¦91137 their contributions with Barnabas¦91143 and Saul¦91145 to take to the elders¦91140.
\c 12
\s1 Persecution of believers restarts
\rem /s1 More Persecution; Peter's Miraculous Escape From Prison; James Killed and Peter Imprisoned; James Is Killed and Peter Is Imprisoned
\p
\v 1 Around that time¦91150, King¦91156 Herod¦91154 \add Agrippa\add* used his power to mistreat¦91160 some of the believers from the assembly¦91165,
\v 2 and¦91171 he had Yacob¦91172, the brother¦91174 of Yohan¦91175, executed by the sword¦91176.
\v 3 Then¦91179 when he saw¦91178 that it pleased¦91181 the Jewish religious leaders, he went on to seize Peter¦91194 during the \it Flat Bread¦91200 Celebration\it*.
\v 4 After being arrested¦91204, Peter was put¦91205 in prison¦91208 where he was guarded¦91215 by four squads¦91213 of four soldiers¦91214 each. After the Passover¦91220 Feast¦91220, Herod planned to display Peter to the people¦91225,
\v 5 but while he was being¦91230 held in prison¦91233, those in the assembly¦91249 were earnestly¦91241 asking God¦91229 to help him¦91255.
\s1 A messenger leads Peter out of prison
\rem /s1 Peter Is Set Free from Prison; Peter Delivered from Prison; Peter's Miraculous Escape from Prison
\p
\v 6 Herod¦91266 planned to send for Peter later that evening, but¦91257 meanwhile Peter had¦91277 fallen¦91273 asleep¦91273 chained with two chains between¦91274 two soldiers¦91276. There were also prison¦91291 guards¦91280 at the door¦91287
\v 7 but¦91292 one of \nd Yahweh's\nd* messengers¦91294 \add suddenly appeared\add* standing¦91296 by Peter and¦91292 light¦91300 radiated through the prison¦91305 cell¦91305. The messenger¦91294 poked Peter in the side¦91310 to wake him up, saying¦91315, “Quickly, get up!” The chains¦91323 fell¦91320 off his¦91321 wrists
\v 8 and the messenger said, “Get dressed and put on your sandals¦91341,” so he did¦91343. Then¦91329 the messenger said, “Now put on your coat¦91351 and follow¦91354 me.”
\v 9 So¦91356 Peter followed¦91358 the messenger¦91371 out of the cell, not really knowing¦91362 if it was real or if he was still dreaming.
\v 10 They went past the first¦91379 guard¦91380 and then the second¦91382, and then came¦91384 to the iron¦91389 gate which led¦91391 out of the prison into the city¦91394. The gate opened¦91397 by itself and they went out onto the street, then at the end of the street the messenger¦91415 suddenly left him¦91417.
\p
\v 11 By now Peter¦91420 was fully awake and said¦91426 to himself¦91424, “Now I know¦91428 that the \nd master¦91434\nd* really did send¦91432 his¦91437 messenger¦91436 to rescue¦91439 me from Herod¦91443 and from the plans of the Jewish leaders.”
\p
\v 12 Now that he realised this, he went¦91456 to Maria's¦91461 house¦91459 (the mother¦91463 of Yohan¦91464 Markos¦91468 \add !/ John¦91464 Mark¦91468\add*) where¦91469 many believers had met to pray.
\v 13 He knocked¦91475 at the door¦91482 in the fence and¦91477 a servant¦91487 girl¦91487 named Rhoda¦91491 came out to see who it was.
\v 14 But¦91493 when she recognised¦91494 Peter's voice¦91496, she was so excited that she forgot about opening¦91503 the door, but¦91493 ran¦91507 back inside to tell everyone that Peter was standing¦91510 out there.
\v 15 They told her¦91522 that she must be raving¦91525 mad¦91525, but she insisted¦91528 it was true, but they said¦91524 that it must be his¦91542 messenger¦91539.
\p
\v 16 Meanwhile Peter¦91545 continued¦91546 knocking¦91547, and when they eventually opened¦91549 the outer door, they saw¦91552 that it¦91549 was him¦91554 and they were amazed.
\v 17 But¦91582 Peter signalled them with his hand¦91563 to be quiet, and then¦91582 he explained how the \nd master¦91575\nd* had led¦91577 him¦91576 out of the prison¦91580, and instructed them, “Tell this to Yacob and the brothers¦91588.” Then¦91582 he left and went off to another¦91594 place¦91595.
\p
\v 18 Once daylight came, there¦91599 was pandemonium among¦91603 the soldiers¦91605 \add in the prison as they tried to figure out\add* what had¦91596 happened to Peter¦91609.
\v 19 Then¦91613 when King Herod¦91611 sent for Peter and he wasn't there, the prison guards¦91621 were interrogated and then¦91613 taken away to be executed.
\rem /s1 Herod's Death; The Death of Herod Agrippa
\p After that, Herod left Yudea¦91629 and went up to Caesarea¦91632 to stay¦91633.
\s1 The death of Herod
\p
\v 20 Now King¦91667 Herod was disputing with the people of Tyre¦91641 and Tsidon, and so they got together and persuaded¦91659 Blastos¦91660, a close personal servant of the king, to be their¦91674 spokesman in asking for peace¦91670 because¦91671 they were dependent on food from the king's provinces.
\p
\v 21 On the agreed day¦91686, Herod¦91688, dressed¦91689 in his royal¦91691 garments and¦91685 seated on his throne, started to address¦91697 them.
\v 22 The crowd shouted out, “This is the voice¦91710 of a \nd god¦91709\nd*, not of a man.”
\v 23 Because¦91724 he didn't¦91726 attribute the honour to \nd God¦91731\nd*, one of the \nd Yahweh's\nd* messengers¦91722 immediately¦91717 struck¦91720 him¦91721 down and¦91718 he stopped¦91743 breathing¦91743 as a result of a worm infestation.
\p
\v 24 Meanwhile God's message¦91746 continued to spread and¦91752 multiply¦91753.
\p
\v 25 By then¦91755 Barnabas¦91754 and Saul¦91757 had completed their ministry and returned to\f + \fr 12:25 \ft TD:Some manuscripts have ‘from’ here because in the next few sentences it seems that they were returned to Antioch.\f* Yerushalem¦91763 taking¦91767 Yohan¦91770 Markos¦91774 (John Mark) along¦91767 with them.
\c 13
\s1 The spirit chooses Barnabas and Saul
\rem /s1 Barnabas and Saul Are Chosen and Sent; Barnabas and Saul Are Sent Out; Paul's work among the Gentiles; Barnabas and Saul Commissioned
\p
\v 1 In the assembly¦91783 at Antioch¦91779 there¦91775 were some prophets¦91784 and teachers¦91786: Barnabas¦91791, Simeon¦91793 (called¦91796 Niger¦91797), Lucius¦91799 from Cyrene¦91801, Manaen¦91802 (who grew up with Herod¦91804 the tetrarch), and Saul¦91810.
\v 2 One day when they were ministering¦91811 to the \nd master¦91815\nd* and fasting¦91817, the holy¦91822 \nd spirit¦91820\nd* said¦91818, Appoint Barnabas¦91828 and Saul¦91831 to serve me and do the work¦91834 that¦91835 I have¦91836 called¦91836 them to.”
\v 3 So they¦91848 fasted¦91839 and prayed¦91841 and placed¦91844 their¦91845 hands¦91846 on the two, and then sent¦91848 them off.
\s1 Barnabas and Saul go to Cyprus to preach
\rem /s1 On Cyprus; The Apostles Preach in Cyprus; Paul's First Missionary Journey
\p
\v 4 So¦91853 Barnabas and Saul, having¦91854 been sent¦91854 by the holy¦91859 \nd spirit¦91860\nd*, went¦91862 down to Seleucia¦91867 \add at the coast\add* and from there¦91868 sailed¦91871 on to \add the island of\add* Cyprus¦91874.
\v 5 When¦91875 they arrived in \add the town of\add* Salamis¦91881, they proclaimed¦91884 God's message¦91887 in the \add ≈Jewish¦91893 meeting¦91893 halls¦91893\add*. They also had Yohan¦91900 as their assistant.
\s1 Sergius believes after Bar-Jesus is blinded
\p
\v 6 They travelled around the island¦91911 and when they got to Pafos¦91913, they met a Jewish man¦91916 named Bar-Jesus.\f + \fr 13:6 \ft The Greek form of his name was Elymas according to verse 8.\f* He was a sorcerer and false¦91920 prophet¦91920
\v 7 who was with Sergius Paulus the proconsul¦91934, an intelligent¦91938 man. Sergius sent for Barnabas¦91942 and¦91943 Saul¦91944 because he wanted to hear¦91948 God's message¦91950 from them,
\v 8 but¦91954 the sorcerer opposed them and tried to prevent Sergius¦91956 from believing.
\v 9 So then Saul¦91976 (the \add Roman\add* form of his name was Paul¦91980), filled¦91981 with the holy¦91983 \nd spirit¦91982\nd* looked¦91985 intently¦91985 at Bar-Jesus
\v 10 and said¦91988, “You're full¦91990 of all kinds of deceit¦91992 and fraud¦91996 you child of the devil¦91999. Will you never stop twisting the truth about following the \nd master¦92009\nd*?
\v 11 Well, look here! \nd Yahweh¦92019\nd* will extend his power against you and blind¦92024 you—you'll go¦92046 a season¦92031 without seeing¦92026 the sun¦92028!”
\p And immediately¦92032 he could only see¦92015 fog and darkness¦92044, and needed someone to guide him¦92041 around¦92046 by the hand.
\v 12 The proconsul¦92053 believed¦92058 when he saw¦92050 what had happened, and was amazed¦92061 as he learnt about the \nd master¦92067\nd*.
\s1 Paul and Barnabas in Pisidia
\rem /s1 In Pisidian Antioch; In Antioch in Pisidia; Paul Preaches in Antioch of Pisidia; Paul and Barnabas in Antioch of Pisidia
\p
